ritize  these largest most important customers  what ways can we think of to reduce the  cost of sales for the long term for the  end of the sole curve where the moment  we're actually  even losing money also did a couple of  purchasing projects and here this is one  of the first standard analysis as well  so looking at the supplier base and  you're asking yourself how is the spend  of the company  distributed among the suppliers and  again  often you also see this strong  concentration of a spend with a couple  of suppliers and then this  big long tail and here often again the  question is how can we optimize this can  we consolidate some of the spend of the  suppliers  in the long tail with larger suppliers  to simplify the organization and  potentially also get  volume discounts next example a project  where we looked into the product  portfolio of a company  again same thing per rate analysis you  notice that a small share of the  products create the vast majority of the  revenue  and the question then is what can we do  with the long tail now of course to not  be misunderstood here this parade  analysis is a very basic tool  it's very quick and easy to do it in the  very beginning this will of course  not be the major insight of such a  project this will not be the end of it  all but it's often a good  effective first starting point to get  for yourself also good understanding of  how this business is structured and  potentially you can also spark some  first discussions with your client  counterparts or colleagues about certain  topics that you no further want to look  into into your project  but before we jump into it i want to  introduce you to the sponsor of today's  video  and this sponsor is skillshare  skillshare is an online learning  community with thousands of classes for  creative and curious people you can  explore new skills  deepen your passions and get lost in  creativity there are classes on  marketing personal  branding presentation skills and 